# Node: or.ByKnownOrFact with stored equality transport
#
# Before:
# forall a, b, c R:
#     a = b
#     b = c
#     a > 0 or a < 0
#     =>:
#         c > 0 or c < 0
# Former behavior: this verified, but Known Or retained only the source Or
# FactId; argument matching omitted the generating equality citations.
#
# Now: the same proof retains an equality certificate for each argument.
# Both occurrences of c cite the a = b, b = c path; zero uses identity.
forall a, b, c R:
    a = b
    b = c
    a > 0 or a < 0
    =>:
        c > 0 or c < 0

# Boundary: an unrelated argument or changed branch condition cannot reuse
# the stored Or. Nested alpha identity preserves free owners and carriers.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/or/by_known_or_fact/stored_equality_transport.lit
# Producer/boundary tests: known_or_nested_binders_tests
# Consumers: detailed_known_or_preserves_each_argument_equality_path and
# graph_known_or_transport_keeps_both_equality_dependencies.
